8. Predict the Output – Array Sum
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
int main() {
int a[] = {5, 10, 15, 20};
int sum = 0;

for(int i = 0; i &lt; 4; i++) {
sum += a[i];
}
printf(&quot;%d&quot;, sum);
return 0;
}
Question: Predict the output and determine the time complexity.
 Array Sum
Array:
5 10 15 20
Calculation:
sum = 0
sum = 0 + 5  = 5
sum = 5 + 10 = 15
sum = 15 + 15 = 30
sum = 30 + 20 = 50
Output:
50
Time complexity: O(n)
Because the loop visits every array element once.
For this particular array, n = 4, but generally:
O(n)
